     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin in adults (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you check what was intended? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, split into divided doses\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd still recommend a pharmacist review first."
      }
     ],
